ic survey, a drilling program, and collection of talus fines and rock chip samples for geochemistry.","platform":"ground","line_km":60.0},{"method":"magnetics","page":105,"text":"of talus fine sampling, 1:10,000 geological and structural mapping, ground magnetic geophysical surveying, and satellite-borne hyperspectral and structural analysis.","platform":"ground","year":2020},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":106,"text":"Highlights include a large >1 by 1-km resistivity-low (conductivity-high) target located between Altar Central and Altar East within a larger 3 by 3-km resistivity anomaly that includes the be","year":2021},{"method":"magnetotellurics","page":106,"text":"\u2013 3D IP and Magneto-Telluric (MT) Survey: Phases I and II of a 3D IP and MT survey was completed during the 2020-2021 field season.","year":2020},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":107,"text":"The results of the 3D IP/Resistivity and MT geophysical surveys (see Company news release, dated June 13, 2022) completed across the entire Altar project revealed a compelling","year":2022},{"method":"magnetics","page":444,"text":"High quality data sets available on site include ground magnetics, 3D IP and 3D MT geophysics, as well as geological and structural mapping, state of the art, property wide talus fine surface geochemistr","platform":"ground"}],"targets":[{"page":103,"explained":false,"untested":true,"text":"It is noted the previous magnetic survey performed by Rio Tinto did not contain sufficient resolution for detailed drill target definition. The magnetic reduced-to-pole and vertical derivative maps from the Quantec were utilized in targeting the DDH since the "},{"page":106,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"resistivity-low (conductivity-high) target located between Altar Central and Altar East within a larger 3 by 3-km resistivity anomaly that includes the better grade mineralization from historical drilling at Altar Central and East."},{"page":107,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"Hole ALD-22-222 was drilled in an area with no previous drilling and was designed to test a favorable geophysical signature coincident with a strong, multi-element talus fines geochemical anomaly at surface. Drill hole ALD-22-222 was terminated at 1,226 m dept"}]},"rock":{"rqd":{"n":1,"min":55.0,"max":55.0,"median":55.0,"page":249,"text":"The leached cap and supergene zones show moderate quality, with average RQD values about 55%. Variability in observed fracture frequency was supported through core photo review, to understand spatial variability considerations"},"slope_angle_deg":{"n":1,"min":36.0,"max":36.0,"median":36.0,"page":410,"text":"2. Geotechnical Stability: The assumed overall slope angle of 36 degrees, including ramps, reflects a conservative approach to pit design."}},"model_params":{"block":[15.0,15.0,15.0],"composite_m":15.0,"radius_m":200.0,"top_cut":55.0,"default_cutoff":0.18,"method":"idw","power":2.0,"nsr":{"factors":{"Au":0.32151,"Ag":0.0166},"units":{"Au":"g/t","Ag":"g/t"},"currency":"US$","approximate":null,"source":"NSR and Equivalent gold calculations for QDM are: NSR in Oxide = (1500 \u2013 6.0) x 0.40 x 0.975 x 0.32151 x Au + (20 \u2013 0.55) x 0.51 * 0.975 x 0.032151 x Ag NSR in Sulphide = (1500 \u2013 6.0) x 0.70 x 0.975 x"},"metallurgy":{"routes":["flotation","heap_leach","sx_ew","magnetic"],"traits":["sulphide","arsenic"],"recoveries":{"Cu":87.8,"Au":57.0,"Ag":50.0},"summary":"sulphide ore, arsenic-bearing; processed by flotation to concentrate, then heap leach, then SX-EW, then magnetic separation; stated recovery Cu 87.8%, Au 57%, Ag 50%"},"deposit_style":"vein","value_cutoff":13.99},"effective_date":"2025-09-01","resource":{"page":29,"contained_unit":"oz","categories":{"Measured":{"tonnes":320500000,"grade":0.48,"contained":4946071},"Indicated":{"tonnes":467300000,"grade":0.53,"contained":7962743},"Inferred":{"tonnes":203000000,"grade":0.42,"contained":2741173}},"year":2025,"by_header":true,"cutoff":null,"cutoff_unit":null,"grad